# カエルの為に鐘は鳴る (Kaeru no Tame ni Kane wa Naru, Game Boy, GB-7F805941): the characters of its font by code, as
# the page's list holds them (two bytes, big-endian). The kana follow one plan, seen on the first pages' lists:
# hiragana in the order of the fifty sounds from 0x000, small ones from 0x02E, voiced from 0x037 and half-voiced
# from 0x04B; katakana the same from 0x050 (small 0x07E, voiced 0x087, half-voiced 0x09B). The signs, digits
# (from 0x0D0) and kanji (from 0x0E0) were read in play, a page's codes beside what its screen showed.
